; Sharp PC-1600  --  system ROM, Page 1 / Bank 3 (4000H-7FFFH), OLD revision
; ROM file: PC-1600-ROM/dumps/old/PC1600-P1-B3.BIN  (MD5 ded92d8280f8f83ce3498fb9cbfb9b3d)
; Generated by tools/romdis/build.py from disasm/old/PC1600-P1-B3/PC1600-P1-B3.ann -- edit the
; .ann file, not this one.  Reassembles byte-identical with z80asm.
; ============================================================================
; OLD REVISION (PEEK #(0,&7FFF) = 130). Ported from the NEW revision's knowledge base
; with tools/romdis/annport.py and checked by hand; notes/PC1600-Old-vs-New.md lists the
; differences. Annotations of code that exists only in the NEW revision are left out.
;
; OVERVIEW
; Bank 3, the normal image of the CS24 chip's second half (port 3DH b2 = 1), visible at
; 4000H-7FFFH when port 31H selects bank 3 for page 1. It is called like a ROM module
; (header at 4000H: reset functions, RAM-disk IOCS, AUTORUN search, device table, file
; handler) and hosts the IM2 interrupt dispatcher (4021H). Code in other banks reaches it
; through RST 18H to 4000H-7FFFH (BANKJP sets port 3DH := 04H); most P0-B0 jump-table
; entries for display, 1500 mode, slots and power go to the jump table at
; 4024H-40CCH. Contents: interrupt dispatcher, LCD character output, keyboard matrix scan
; and key translation, RAM-disk driver and file system (S1:/S2:), COM: file driver and
; serial receive interrupt, PC-1500 (LH5803) CPU switch and 1500 display / math / token
; calls, CALL/OUT/POKE/HEXNUM, work-area allocation, memory map (SSLOTMP, SLOTST,
; APOTST), POWER, WAKE$, EOF/LOF/LOC/DSKF, and the kanji input and font
; code for the JAPAN ROM.
; ============================================================================

